commit 06d779ebc567f301f4a0e4346196226db33133b4
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 09:05:03 2026 +0000

    Festival data layer: fetcher -> raw per edition/source -> converter -> serving block; Jerusalem re-homed

    Festivals have editions and several required sources each, so raw now lives
    in edition-aware, per-source folders (data/festivals/<festival>/<edition>/
    <source>/, with a manifest), fetched by hand only. Only the converter
    (scraper/convert/) knows our information requirements: per-source adapters
    turn raw into partials, merge.py combines them by declared precedence and
    records which source won each field, schema.py validates the whole block
    before anything is written, and writes are atomic and limited to the
    requested edition. `to_serving.py --check` re-derives every committed serving
    file from committed raw in verify.sh.

    Jerusalem moves to scraper/festivals/jerusalem/ (festival.toml, a site source
    and a nominatim source, curated venue research). Its raw is re-homed from the
    committed catalogue, not re-fetched (the site is unreachable here; the
    manifests say so). The converter still writes site/data/jerusalem/shows.json,
    byte-identical, for /planJerusalem/; site/shared/festival-catalogue.js loads
    the new block into the exact in-memory shape the planner uses today.

    Closes #845

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
